      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Synergistic redox interactions among mixed transition-metal cations govern the enhanced OER activity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mixed-cation redox interactions dynamically modulate surface binding energies.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The material is epitaxial LaCr0.2Mn0.2Fe0.2Co0.2Ni0.2O3-δ with a (001) surface facet.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing a single B-site cation composition with a multication B-site composition changes the intrinsic OER activity.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The multication composition enables simultaneous oxidation and reduction of different metal centers during intermediate adsorption.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The compared catalysts can be prepared with identical morphology and crystallographic orientation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Multiple transition-metal oxidation states are dynamically modulated at the catalyst surface during OER.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adsorption of OER intermediates causes different cations in the multication material to undergo oxidation or reduction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooperative cation redox changes lower adsorption-energy barriers.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooperative cation redox changes facilitate more efficient charge transfer during OER.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed cooperative redox behavior is absent from single-B-site catalysts.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Single-B-site parent perovskites roughly follow expected volcano-type OER activity trends.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-entropy perovskite produces 17 to 680 times higher current at a fixed overpotential than its single-B-site parent compounds.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The enhanced current is correlated with detectable dynamic oxidation-state changes in the constituent metals.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using epitaxial samples supports attribution of the activity difference to intrinsic composition rather than uncontrolled structure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10061923::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is expected to apply to well-defined epitaxial surfaces with controlled morphology under OER conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
